# The tutorial video's gameplay: a whole first run, from the main menu to a pair of new boots.
#
# Player commands only (this runs under --record), with the real model writing every passage. The
# launch flags, what each section relies on and every known fragility are in NOTES.md beside this
# file. In short: the world is Fenumoth (moon 5, a sylvan world), the childhood is pinned to the port
# city, the dock work, the sword and the dream of the golden arch (--childhood-path), the two journeys
# each meet one wolf (--force-encounter), the farmer and the cobbler are found where the script expects
# them (--start-area, --npc-static, --observe-only), the farmer offers only the farmhand's post
# (--job-only) and the two wills (diligence, provisioning) make the asking and the buying a single
# thought each. Every roll a script cannot foresee is settled with the humors the player really holds
# (--humors all=voluptas), spent with `click humor <queue> needed` / `click die needed`, which press
# only while the roll is still failing.
#
# Model waits are long on purpose (a passage takes a minute or more on a CPU); the cut fast-forwards
# them. `clip` names follow the brief's outline; `hold`s are where the narration will speak.
#
# FLAGS: --childhood-path "sobs,waves,sharp,golden arch,shelter" --force-encounter wolf,wolf --no-encounters
#        --npc-static --start-area "Longhouse Hall,Cobbler's Shop" --observe-only "farmer,cobbler"
#        --npc-affinity DistantAcquaintance --grant-mm diligence,provisioning,swordsmanship:2
#        --job-only farmhand --humors all=voluptas

# The narrowing flags name the farm's and the city's rooms and people; the childhood, the get-up and
# the world map have none of them, which is expected.
allow-flag-miss --start-area
allow-flag-miss --observe-only

# ── New run ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The model loads before the menu is offered.
wait mode MainMenu 900
mark new_run
clip new_run
cursor rest
hold 3
click menu New
wait mode WorldSelection 60
clip end new_run

# ── Select a world ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The sky is drawn from a constant, so Fenumoth is the same moon, in the same place, on every machine
# — and it is in view without turning the sky (under --record a moon must be on screen to be clicked).
# Hold on the sky (world generation, history, the lore), point at two other moons, pick Fenumoth and
# read its box.
mark world_selection
clip world_selection
cursor rest
hold 5
point moon Isholmir
hold 3
point moon Halarriel
hold 3
click moon Fenumoth
wait 120
cursor rest
hold 6
click world confirm
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 900
clip end world_selection

# ── Protagonist creation: the organs, grouped by the system each one feeds ─────────────────────────
# `point element organ:<part>` hovers a part (its description and the stats it drives show on the
# right); `click element organ:<part>` raises it by one point of the 25. The grouping and the code
# behind it are in NOTES.md.
mark creation
clip creation_overview
cursor rest
hold 5
clip end creation_overview

# Thinking and memory: noetic points, the memory modules, mental maps, doubt.
mark organs_thinking
clip organs_thinking
point element organ:anamnesis
hold 3
click element organ:anamnesis
hold 2
point element organ:cerebrum
hold 3
click element organ:cerebrum
click element organ:cerebrum
hold 2
point element organ:cerebellum
hold 3
click element organ:cerebellum
click element organ:cerebellum
hold 2
point element organ:hippocampus
hold 3
point element organ:pineal_gland
hold 3
clip end organs_thinking

# The senses: initiative in a fight, the nose's warning of encounters, and what can be observed.
mark organs_senses
clip organs_senses
point element organ:left_eye
hold 3
point element organ:right_eye
hold 2
point element organ:left_ear
hold 3
click element organ:left_ear
click element organ:right_ear
hold 2
point element organ:nose
hold 3
clip end organs_senses

