click die needed
click humor pulmones needed
click die needed
click humor paunch needed
click die needed
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
hold 2
click continue
advance 20 900
cursor rest
hold 4
click button
wait mode WorldView 900
clip end get_up

# ── A run begins ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mark run_start
clip run_start
cursor rest
hold 5
clip end run_start

# The protagonist screen, the way a player opens it: Escape, then Protagonist.
pause
wait 30
click menu Protagonist
wait 30

mark anatomy
clip anatomy
click tab anatomy
wait 10
cursor rest
hold 6
clip end anatomy

mark memory
clip memory
click tab memory
wait 10
cursor rest
hold 6
clip end memory

# The inventory: the sword in hand, the cloak and clothes, the backpack. Open the backpack and eat
# the bread in it.
mark inventory
clip inventory
click tab inventory
wait 10
cursor rest
hold 5
click element backpack
wait 5
hold 3
click element content:bread
wait 5
cursor rest
hold 4
click element consume
wait 5
hold 3
clip end inventory

# The humors: the bread's humors have entered the paunch at the spiral's mouth (index 0 is the
# newest). Pointing at it shows what it is and what it does to a die.
mark humors
clip humors
click tab humors
wait 10
cursor rest
hold 5
point element humor:paunch:0
hold 6
point element humor:paunch:1
hold 4
cursor rest
hold 3
clip end humors

click back
wait 30
click menu Continue
wait mode WorldView 60

# ── Travel to the farm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mark travel_farm
clip travel_farm
travel 7011
wait 10
cursor rest
hold 4
travel-go
wait mode EncounterPrompt 900
clip end travel_farm

# ── The first fight: a wolf on the road ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# --force-encounter puts a wolf on this journey's middle step. The fight is seeded end to end (the
# arena from the run's GameRng, the wolf from the travel generator, every roll from the fight's own
# stream), so its course is the same on every replay whatever the model wrote before it: the wolf
# starts far off and needs two of our turns to close, then falls to the fifth snap thrust. Our own
# turns are ended to let it come; it never lands a blow.
mark fight_1
clip fight_1
cursor rest
hold 4
click engage
wait mode Fighting 60
cursor rest
hold 5
regions
# Turns 1 and 2: wait for the wolf.
click end-turn
wait 120
cursor rest
hold 3
click end-turn
wait 120
cursor rest
hold 3
# Turn 1: a snap thrust with the short sword (the skill group opens first; it closes again after
# every action). Humors are spent only if the roll is failing.
click skill Short Sword
wait 5
click skill Snap Thrust
wait 5
click fighter enemy
wait 60
cursor rest
hold 3
dice
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
click humor spleen needed
click die needed
click humor pulmones needed
click die needed
click humor paunch needed
click die needed
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
hold 2
click continue
wait 60
cursor rest
hold 3
click end-turn
wait 120
cursor rest
hold 3
